    {"parameters":{"content":"## Part of the JobOps Template\n\nThis is the router. In live use, *i.e.*, someone actually messaging the bot, chatId is read automatically from the incoming message, no setup needed.\n\n**If you test/execute this workflow standalone** (not by sending a real Telegram message), there is no incoming message to read chatId from, so downstream sub-workflow calls need a chat ID supplied manually as test input. \nFind yours: message this template's bot once → click the **JobOps Template Bot Trigger** node → **Listen for test event** → send another message → read `message.chat.id` from the captured output.\n\nSee **JobOps Template - Application Reminders** and **JobOps Template - Reviews Digest** for the two workflows that always need a real chat ID hardcoded (they're cron-triggered, no incoming message at all).","height":436,"width":576,"color":"#DC8ADD"},"id":"b2f4ba2a-bc8a-4fb0-80d1-f21d75a110dd","name":"Setup Note - Chat ID","type":"n8n-nodes-base.stickyNote","typeVersion":1,"position":[0,-144]}
